// Lesson template v4 (docs/COURSE_DESIGN_COMMUNICATIVE.md §12). One storyline, the cast a year after the B1 course
// (docs/COURSE_CAST.md): Oskar (10, 4.b, Kase kool) asks for his first social-media account and the family makes a
// digital agreement; at Tuul Logistika Sofia leads the introduction of the AI planning tool „TarkPlaan” (vendor's
// trainer Joonas Vaino, data protection specialist Mirjam Kõiv) and its new data rules, Gert fears for his night shift;
// Viktor learns Smart-ID at Eneli's library course, gets a phishing call and reports it (bank adviser Allan); a faked
// screenshot about the new girl Lenna spreads in the 4.b class chat while Helgi forwards a fake Smart-ID „news” to the
// family group (her neighbour Ilmar already „renewed”). One goal said on the first sheet: at the end the learner speaks
// at the 4.b parents' evening on children's online safety, takes part in the debate (ban or training) and answers the
// board chair Marje Lepp in writing (059).
// Grammar (B2, docs/METHODOLOGY_STANDARD.md §5): nominalisation with -mine / -ja — andmete kogumine, otsuse tegemine,
// asukoha jälgimine, kasutaja, vastutaja; a verb sentence → a noun phrase and back, typical of written and official
// style — taught in 057 (the lecture's noun phrases noticed, rule table, style sorted; transformation both ways, the
// data-rules cloze; the night-shift notice rewritten in plain verbs), back in 058 (notice: PIN-koodide avaldamine =
// PIN-koode ei avaldata). 058 trains the impersonal (grammarPlan), 059 the quotative and hedging (väidetavalt, kooli
// sõnul, olevat) as a spiral of module 10.
// The final shape (docs/COURSE_FINAL_SHAPE_B2.md §4.1 row 12, 2026-10-29): 056 KIRJ L→W (corner W2a = the screen-time
// chart summarised with a comment, W15; main = W13 semi-formal letter to the class teacher), 057 PROJ L→S (corner R1 =
// the problem article „Kas masin võtab meie töö?”, ≈ 520 words, predict and check; main = S16 talk at the project
// meeting, recorded at home), 058 LUGE R→W (corner R4 = the library newsletter with eight sentences and one extra, R16;
// main = the statement to the web constable), 059 RÄÄK R→S (corner W1 = the reply to the board chair, 80–100 words;
// main = S16 talk at the parents' evening). Every teaching lesson: review naming the previous lesson and a module 9–10
// lesson, a pair task in the lesson, a home recording in Kasuta, two fluency tasks; S16 in 057 and 059, S17 in 057 and
// 059. Module 11's words return: eelarve, kulutus, tasuta, reklaam, tarbija, leping, tellimus, laen, kiirlaen, säästud,
// hädaabifond, hüvitama, kaebus, õigus, seadus, tähtaeg, garantii, investeerima, tasub end ära, ettevaatlik, otsus.
//   056 „Linnaelu” measures three families' screen time; Kadri on the radio about children and screens; the school's
//       screen-time survey; the family council on Oskar's account, a voice message to Helgi, a letter to Kristel Saar.
//   057 Joonas Vaino's lecture on TarkPlaan (noun phrases); Mirjam's data rules (cloze), an article on AI at work, the
//       Sofia–Gert debate with argument cards; the project meeting with three position cards, Sofia's talk, Gert's notice.
//   058 The library's guide to Smart-ID and phishing calls; Viktor's case in the library newsletter (sentence bank,
//       forms text); his recording and Allan's voice message, the call to the bank's fraud line, a report to the police.
//   059 Three sources (screenshot, family-group „news”, the school's notice); an article on why false news spreads;
//       the parents' evening: Kristel Saar's invitation and survey, the talk, the debate and the reply to Marje Lepp.
